{
  "case_id": "2022-22-179",
  "document_hash": "e43440bd8c8668b44b73d6a5ccfe1c4c3592903ee3965a202f339cf9604bae15",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Supreme Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-179",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e43440bd8c8668b44b73d6a5ccfe1c4c3592903ee3965a202f339cf9604bae15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e43440bd8c86-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:46 a.m.\nAPPEARANCES:\nBRIAN H. FLETCHER, Principal Deputy Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nESHA BHANDARI, ESQUIRE, New York, New York; on behalf of the Respondent.\nHeritage Reporting Corporation"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2022-22-179",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e43440bd8c8668b44b73d6a5ccfe1c4c3592903ee3965a202f339cf9604bae15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e43440bd8c86-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For more than a century, Congress has made it a crime to encourage or induce certain immigration offenses. Mr. Hansen violated that statute by inducing noncitizens to reside in the United States illegally so that he could take their money in a fraudulent citizenship scheme.\nNo one suggests that that conduct was protected by the First Amendment. But the Ninth Circuit invoked the overbreadth doctrine to facially invalidate this longstanding statute by giving the words \"encourage\" and \"induce\" their broadest possible meaning and sweeping in wide swaths of protected speech."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-22-179",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e43440bd8c8668b44b73d6a5ccfe1c4c3592903ee3965a202f339cf9604bae15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e43440bd8c86-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Are you aware of any instance in which the -- this section has been applied in the way that the Ninth Circuit hypothesized?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-22-179",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e43440bd8c8668b44b73d6a5ccfe1c4c3592903ee3965a202f339cf9604bae15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e43440bd8c86-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: How can you say the first part is invalid and still keep a second part?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-22-179",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e43440bd8c8668b44b73d6a5ccfe1c4c3592903ee3965a202f339cf9604bae15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e43440bd8c86-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: How is this different from that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Bhandari",
      "case_id": "2022-22-179",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e43440bd8c8668b44b73d6a5ccfe1c4c3592903ee3965a202f339cf9604bae15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e43440bd8c86-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Hansen should prevail here for three reasons. The government concedes that the statute is unconstitutional under its plain meaning. Instead, it asks this Court to rewrite the statute to prohibit only solicitation and aiding and abetting."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-22-179",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e43440bd8c8668b44b73d6a5ccfe1c4c3592903ee3965a202f339cf9604bae15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e43440bd8c86-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Is speech the only component of the First Amendment subject to overbreadth?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Bhandari",
      "case_id": "2022-22-179",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e43440bd8c8668b44b73d6a5ccfe1c4c3592903ee3965a202f339cf9604bae15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e43440bd8c86-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress removed the narrower verbs, \"solicit\" and \"assist,\" and left in the broader verbs, \"encourage\" and \"induce.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-22-179",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e43440bd8c8668b44b73d6a5ccfe1c4c3592903ee3965a202f339cf9604bae15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e43440bd8c86-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Encouraging someone to engage in prostitution is not necessarily -- criminalizing that is not necessarily unconstitutional, it just has to satisfy strict scrutiny, and you would apply the same thing here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-22-179",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e43440bd8c8668b44b73d6a5ccfe1c4c3592903ee3965a202f339cf9604bae15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e43440bd8c86-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Encouraging someone to commit suicide?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2022-22-179",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e43440bd8c8668b44b73d6a5ccfe1c4c3592903ee3965a202f339cf9604bae15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e43440bd8c86-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the government could claim a compelling interest."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Reporters Committee for Freedom of the Press",
      "case_id": "2022-22-179",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e43440bd8c8668b44b73d6a5ccfe1c4c3592903ee3965a202f339cf9604bae15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e43440bd8c86-0003-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the amicus brief from the Reporters Committee for Freedom of the Press noted. The government doesn't treat Section 1324 as a dead letter. It's still available to open investigations even if they never charge someone."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-22-179",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e43440bd8c8668b44b73d6a5ccfe1c4c3592903ee3965a202f339cf9604bae15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e43440bd8c86-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Did I understand you to say, once you give that up, then this is okay because they can criminalize all civil violations?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-22-179",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e43440bd8c8668b44b73d6a5ccfe1c4c3592903ee3965a202f339cf9604bae15",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e43440bd8c86-0004-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I -- I would like to know where to draw that line."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2022-22-179",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "e43440bd8c8668b44b73d6a5ccfe1c4c3592903ee3965a202f339cf9604bae15",
